      "type": "FIXTURE_CREW",
      "transition": "zoom",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "First though — where does being logged in actually live? Not in the page. It's cookies and local storage, and both of those sit in the context. The dressing room, from episode eight. Which turns out to be very handy indeed, because a context is one single thing. And one single thing can be picked up, saved, and carried somewhere else entirely.",
