    {
      "id": "s10",
      "type": "CODE_RUN",
      "transition": "push",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "So here's step one, and you run this exactly once, ever. Log in for real, like a person would — email, password, click the button. Nothing clever so far. Then that last line is the entire trick. Storage state writes those cookies and that local storage into a plain JSON file. That file? That's your hand stamp.",
      "data": {
        "codeRun": {
          "filename": "save_stamp.py",
          "language": "py",
          "resultLabel": "what you get",
          "color": "green",
          "atWord": 2.75,
          "caption": "log in for real. once.",
          "lines": [
            {
              "text": "# save_stamp.py — run this ONCE"
            },
            {
              "text": "page.get_by_label(\"Email\").fill(",
              "detail": "a real login, like a person",
              "sub": "typed into the real form",
              "label": "login",
              "atWord": 12.583
            },
            {
              "text": "    \"neo@matrix.io\")"
            },
            {
              "text": "page.get_by_label(\"Password\").fill(",
              "detail": "then the password, same as always",
              "sub": "nothing clever happening here",
              "label": "creds",
              "atWord": 18
            },
            {
              "text": "    \"redpill\")"
            },
            {
              "text": "page.get_by_role(\"button\",",
              "detail": "and press the button",
              "sub": "you are properly in now",
              "label": "in",
              "atWord": 25.167
            },
            {
              "text": "    name=\"Sign in\").click()"
            },
            {
              "text": ""
            },
            {
              "text": "context.storage_state(",
              "detail": "now save the stamp to a file",
              "sub": "auth.json, on disk",
              "label": "saved",
              "atWord": 34.083
            },
            {
              "text": "    path=\"auth.json\")"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 632,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-15-auth_long_s10.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "type": "CODE_RUN",
      "transition": "push",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Step two is where the whole thing pays off. Any test that wants in just builds its context with that file attached. Born already stamped. So it goes straight to the dashboard — no login page, no five second toll, nothing at all in between.",
      "data": {
        "codeRun": {
          "filename": "any_test.py",
          "language": "py",
          "resultLabel": "where you land",
          "color": "green",
          "atWord": 2.583,
          "caption": "born stamped, straight to the dashboard",
          "lines": [
            {
              "text": "# every other test"
            },
            {
              "text": "context = browser.new_context(",
              "detail": "hand the stamp to the context",
              "sub": "born already logged in",
              "label": "stamped",
              "atWord": 9.75
            },
            {
              "text": "    storage_state=\"auth.json\")"
            },
            {
              "text": "page = context.new_page()"
            },
